    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4561\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending\nthe authorization of the county of Rensselaer to impose an additional\none percent of sales and compensating use taxes\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation authorizes the imposition of an additional one\npercent sales tax in Rensselaer County until November 30, 2015.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThe bill amends clause 3 of subparagraph (i) of the opening paragraph\nof section 1210 of the tax law, as amended by chapter 224 of the laws\nof 2011 to authorize the continuation of an additional one percent\nsales tax in Rensselaer County until November 30, 2015.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is being introduced at the request of the Rensselaer\nCounty Legislature. Under current law, Rensselaer County is authorized\nto collect an additional one percent sales tax. This is due to expire\non November 30, 2013 (Chapter 224 of the Laws of 2011).  This\nlegislation is necessary to allow Rensselaer County to continue its\ncollection of the additional sales tax.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
